WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.389 --> 00:00:08.220
You can do some pretty amazing things with
sound, fight wars, heal people, even kill

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.220
people.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:14.799
We'll get more into that in a minute, but
first, can an opera singer really shatter

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:23.410
a wine glass with their voice?

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.750
Have you ever done this?

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.370
The sound being emitted from the glass is
what's known as its resonant frequency.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:40.320
That's the the pitch at which an object emits
sound when affected by a physical object.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.570
Every object has a different resonant frequency.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:48.700
It's easier to hear resonance from a wine
glass because its unique bowl shape amplifies

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.230
the sound.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:55.359
So how can an opera singer use this knowledge
to shatter the glass?

00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:01.629
Sound is essentially the compression and rarefaction
of the air around the source, creating pressure

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:07.600
waves, that's why sound can't be heard in
a complete vacuum, because there's no air

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.110
molecules to affect.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:14.000
When you sing you create these pressure waves
on the air around you.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.910
However, if you sing at the exact same pitch
or frequency that the wine glass resonates

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:26.060
at, you will start to create pressure waves
around the glass, and if you sing loud enough

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.240
and long enough you can shatter the glass.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.190
But it will require a lot of lung power, and
since Opera singers excel in this field, they're

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:39.509
the most likely to shatter glass with their
voice.

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:46.020
Okay, so you can obliterate objects with your
voice, that's impressive, but you can do some

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:49.649
even more amazing things with sound.

00:01:49.649 --> 00:01:56.079
Sound can actually be weaponised, the Long
Range Acoustic Device, is a "sound spotlight"

00:01:56.079 --> 00:02:02.880
capable of emitting a beam of sound at a target
hundreds of metres away, up to 150 decibels.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.280
It's used for crowd control, such as breaking
up riots.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:13.400
However they're also used on European cruise
ships to ward off Somali pirates.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:18.310
Sound has also been weaponised on a smaller
scale to take on all those stabby teenagers

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:19.640
running amok.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:23.990
The Mosquito is an anti anti-social behaviour
device.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:29.060
This small speaker can be attached to the
front of shops, railway lines and anywhere

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.500
else you don't want those little rascals loitering
about.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:38.650
The speaker emits an annoying high pitched
noise at 17KHz.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.370
Because our hearing degrades with age, the
Mosquito's high frequency sound waves can

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:49.080
only be heard by teenagers, thus, keeping
them well clear of your property.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:55.640
A similar, yet less obnoxious approach to
fighting minor crime was taken in London.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:00.840
When people hear music they don't like, their
dopamine production is suppressed.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:08.459
In 2003 subway stations in London started
to play classical music and it worked, within

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:13.130
a year and a half, robberies and vandalism
dropped by a third.

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:16.280
But how dangerous can sound get?

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:23.850
Well, theoretically it's possible to kill
someone with sound, albeit rather indirectly.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:30.230
When a bomb explodes the sudden rise in atmospheric
pressure creates what's called blast overpressure,

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:35.549
resulting in an incredibly loud noise being
emitted over a large area, you would't hear

00:03:35.549 --> 00:03:38.050
the noise because your eardrums shatter at
160 decibels.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:46.900
But, at 200 decibels the sound pressure would
be enough to rupture a lung and cause fatal

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.010
internal injuries.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:54.180
This caused confusion in World War 1, when
soldiers were found dead despite having no

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:56.120
external injuries.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.330
This means that all those films you've seen
where the protagonist get's thrown from a

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:07.370
massive explosion and survives are complete
crap, the sound alone would kill them.

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:12.129
However, when controlled, sound pressure can
be used to heal people.

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:19.690
A High-Intensity Focused Ultrasound Transducer
is a device that can focus sound energy to

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.580
such intense levels that it creates heat.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.190
Similar to how kids burn ants with a magnifying
glass.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:32.870
The device can heat an area as small as a
grain of rice to hundreds of degrees.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:38.580
In one study it was able to seal the punctured
lungs of pigs in just 2 minutes.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.770
This new technology means that surgery could
be performed without making any incisions

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:49.860
on the body or using general anaesthesia,
and patients will be able to go home the same

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.070
day.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:57.180
Furthermore it can be used to cure cancer,
by using the HiFU device to heat up and kill

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.730
the cancer cells.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:06.860
The technology was tested on 159 men with
prostate cancer, and after one year 92% of

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:09.440
them did not have recurrence cancer.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.580
Surprisingly you can actually eliminate noise
by adding more noise.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.980
Noise cancellation headphones work on this
exact premise, they have a tiny microphone

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:25.440
on their periphery that constantly monitors
all noise outside your headphones.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:31.030
Usually this noise will have a distant waveform
of peaks and troughs, the earphones internal

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:37.320
circuitry create a new waveform that has peaks
and throughs exactly opposite to the recorded

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:43.250
noise and plays it into your ear, this is
called an anti phase.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:48.370
The antiphase cancels out the background noise
and all you hear is your music.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:55.060
It may seem like a strange concept, that adding
more noise can remove it completely.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:06:00.040
But it's like having -2 and adding 2, you
end up with nothing.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:06.070
A company has designed a system that uses
this technology in restaurants and bars to

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:09.290
cancel out the noisy background drone of customers.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:15.800
It uses an array of over 100 microphones and
speakers concealed behind paintings around

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:17.000
the venue.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:23.190
The microphones record the noise of the customers
and creates an antiphase which is then played

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:29.300
back to the customers via the speakers, cancelling
out the ambient noise.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:34.150
This let's people converse with each other
without having to raise their voices.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:40.780
But if the venue is mostly empty it can also
pump background noise out of the speakers

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.890
to make the place seem busier than it actually
is.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:50.010
However the entire system can cost up to $100,000
to install.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:54.710
Can you guess where the quietest place on
earth is?

00:06:54.710 --> 00:07:00.470
It's a small room in Salford, Manchester,
England, more specifically the anechoic chamber

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.840
at the University of Salford.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:11.910
It's actually a room within a room, steel
and crosshatched buffers that absorb all sound.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.380
The room absorbs 99.9% of all sound, the room's
sound level has been measured at -9.4 decibels,

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:21.930
it's so quiet that you can hear your own internal
organs, and the blood pumping through your

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.250
veins.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.330
The chamber is used for testing low level
noise, such as the hum of a light bulb.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:32.490
But ironically most people find the place
upsetting.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:38.440
No matter where you are there's always a considerate
amount of background noise and our brain's

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.880
are very accustomed to it.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.300
The presence of noise tells our body that
things are working.

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:51.060
However, if you remove all sound then all
your senses heighten and your body goes into

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.710
panic mode.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:08:00.050
On 9/11 despite having no mobile phone reception,
a huge number of hikers mysteriously abandoned

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:01.510
their walks.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:06.360
They hadn't heard about the terrorist attacks,
their brain's were just spooked by the lack

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:10.250
of aeroplane noise and they knew something
was wrong.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:17.070
After 5 minutes in the chamber you start to
notice the smallest sounds such as your scalp

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:23.180
moving across your skull when you frown and
your heart pounding in your chest.

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:28.470
Staying in the chamber for longer than 15
minutes can cause extreme symptoms, such as

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:31.150
nausea and panic attacks.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:36.890
Most people suffer aural hallucinations, this
is when you start hearing sounds that aren't

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:41.979
even there, everything from scraping metal
to voices.

00:08:41.979 --> 00:08:47.830
Apparently nobody can survive 45 minutes in
the room without going insane.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:55.730
But for some unfortunate individuals such
surreal experiences are an everyday occurrence.

00:08:55.730 --> 00:09:02.830
Superior canal dehiscence syndrome is a rare
medical condition, affecting the inner ear.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.240
It amplifies all internal sounds.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:12.170
Sufferers hear their own heartbeat, creaking
joints and other unsavoury internal bodily

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.170
functions.

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:20.630
It can get so bad that the sound of the eyeballs
moving in their sockets sounds like "sandpaper

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:22.060
on wood".

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:26.690
Sound travels at 761.2 mph at sea level.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:31.090
But what happens when you travel faster than
the speed of sound?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:36.880
You experience what's called a sonic boom,
which is an extremely loud thumping sound,

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.920
it also creates a visual phenomenon called
a mach cone.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:46.250
This happens because when an object travels
through the air it creates a series of pressure

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:52.420
waves in front and behind it, similar to how
a boat displaces the water.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:57.430
The faster the object travels the more the
pressure waves are compressed together, because

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:01.000
they can't get out of the way of each other
fast enough.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:08.600
Once you reach 761 mph, otherwise known as
Mach 1, the pressure you've created reaches

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:12.000
a critical mass, creating a shock wave.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:17.240
But you won't hear anything at all, because
you're travelling faster than the speed of

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:22.630
sound, the sound will never reach your ears,
unless you slow down.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:11:03.210
But everyone on the ground will hear.

